r files with no chain or signature.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:** src/integrations/payments.ts:35 — \"\"idempotency-key\": req.idempotencyKey,\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** No checkpoints, recovery logs or replay code exist, so signing and verification do not apply. Payments send an Idempotency-Key, but refund keys differ between paths (executor.ts:122 refund-ID vs eligibility-check.ts:42 deposit-waive-ID), and inbound SMS messageId is never deduplicated (sms-webhook.ts:14), so provider redelivery reruns the agent.\n29\t\n30\t`src/integrations/payments.ts` lines 23–42 (cited lines marked >):\n31\t```\n32\t  23  export const payments = {\n33\t  24    async refundDeposit(\n34\t  25      clinicId: string,\n35\t  26      req: { depositId: string; reason: string; idempotencyKey: string },\n36\t  27      signal?: AbortSignal,\n37\t  28    ): Promise<Refund> {\n38\t  29      const res = await fetch(`${BASE}/deposits/${encodeURIComponent(req.depositId)}/refunds`, {\n39\t  30        method: \"POST\",\n40\t  31        signal,\n41\t  32        headers: {\n42\t  33          authorization: `Bearer ${await key(clinicId)}`,\n43\t  34          \"content-type\": \"application/json\",\n44\t  35>         \"idempotency-key\": req.idempotencyKey,\n45\t  36        },\n46\t  37        body: JSON.stringify({ reason: req.reason, metadata: { source: \"clinic-agent\" } }),\n47\t  38      });\n48\t  39      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`refund failed: ${res.status}`);\n49\t  40      return (await res.json()) as Refund;\n50\t  41    },\n51\t  42  };\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\t## R14.2\n55\t\n56\t**Check:** Recovery verifies them against a key or trust anchor stored separately from the records, and refuses any that fail.\n57\t\n58\t**How to verify:** 1) Find recovery code that loads checkpoints. 2) Check it verifies against a key stored separately and refuses failures. 3) Answer no if the key sits in the same store, verification is skipped, or failure is logged and recovery continues.\n59\t\n